I like the idea of having both of these as options, as I've done
things like this in the past when dealing with troublesome MCMCs.

To add to the mix, we might consider an argument that gives the
initial number of MCMC iterations during which there would be no decay
in the amount of adaptation, as this might be handy in a context in
which one is going to throw out a bunch of burn-in samples anyway.

Let's discuss more in a developers meeting.

