Dear all,

thanks for the exchanges and thank you so much Daniel for the new sampler. I hope I will find time soon to test it and compare it with what I have done.

David, I like your remarks: yes this is a case by case adaptation: I can think of no automaton of these. So yes this can be critocized for this. Yet it seems to be an interesting strategy for example in non-linear hierarchical mdoels wher we obtain different equilibria in the different chains. I will try to put it on the paper in the next weeks. Isn't this stratgey preferable to a one wher we restrict the initial values close to what we think the real equilibrium is? Especially if we fit these parameters on a high number of trajectories and use the fitted values on other trajectories with other initial values?

But yes, if we find algorithms that do it automatically it is much better, I agree. I plan to test Jags and Stan on this. I have also tried other algorithms but no clear good result so far.

At least what I can say is that this strategy seems a litlle more promising on the case at hand than Block sampling!

Sincerely,

frédéric

