Frédéric, provided you still are interested in implementing your own adaptation scheme, then yes, it's straightforward to get the value of logMHR (the log acceptance probability) within the adaptiveProcedure() method.  If I'm understanding your question correctly, then, in fact, it's as simple as passing this variable as a second argument to the adaptiveProcedure() method.  The relevant changes are shown below.

In case I'm not following your question exactly right, then feel free to explain further.

Cheers,
Daniel

RW2 <- nimbleFunction(
    .....

    run = function() {
        timesRan <<- timesRan + 1
        if(timesRan > niterNoUpdateTarget) {

            .....
            if(adaptive & timesRan > niterNoAdaptation)     adaptiveProcedure(jump, logMHR)
        }
    },
    methods = list(
        adaptiveProcedure = function(jump = logical(), logMHR = double()) {
            .....
        },
        .....
    )
)

