Yes, this is a relatively recent change to NIMBLE:

If you are using version 0.6-5 or earlier, then in this situation, you will have to specify values for all of these control parameters.  It's a bit of a nuisance.

Starting in version 0.6-6 (released July 2017), there's been a change to how MCMC samplers manage their control parameters, and the default values for control parameters.  If you use this most recent version of NIMBLE (0.6-6), then you do not have to specify values for all of them, and the default values specified inside the RW2 sampler will be used.

I would suggest you update to the latest version of NIMBLE.

